# .cursorrules - Rules for Cursor IDE

## Project
Production-ready AI starter kit. Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript 5.
Russian market. No foreign payments.

## Stack
- Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript 5
- Tailwind CSS 3, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion
- Zustand, TanStack Query v5, React Hook Form + Zod
- Prisma 5 + PostgreSQL 17
- AI: Groq llama-3.3-70b-versatile via ai SDK v6
- Auth: JWT via jose + bcryptjs (no NextAuth)
- Telegram bot: Telegraf
- Email: Resend
- Analytics: Yandex Metrika (ID: 109390519)
- Payments: YooKassa (Russian market)
- Automation: n8n self-hosted

## Folder structure
- app/            — pages and API routes
- features/       — features (auth, ai-chat, telegram, yookassa)
- shared/         — utilities, lib/
- store/          — Zustand stores
- hooks/          — custom hooks
- entities/       — business entities
- widgets/        — large page blocks
- components/     — reusable components (ui/, analytics/)

## Completed features
- Auth: register/login/logout, JWT, middleware
- AI chat: Groq llama-3.3-70b-versatile
- Telegram bot: /start /help /status
- Telegram Login button
- YooKassa payment integration (code ready)
- n8n webhook automation
- Docker + docker-compose
- GitHub Actions CI/CD
- UI Kit: SectionWrapper, GradientText, Badge, FeatureCard, PricingCard, TestimonialCard, HeroSection
- Landing page: Navbar, Hero, Features, Pricing, Testimonials, FAQ, Footer
- Email: Resend, welcome email, subscription email
- SEO: metadata, Open Graph, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, JSON-LD
- Analytics: Yandex Metrika

## Mandatory rules
- TypeScript everywhere, never use any
- Zod for validation of all incoming data
- try/catch for all async operations
- "use client" only when using hooks or events
- Styles only via Tailwind CSS
- No new npm packages without explicit request
- No Prisma schema changes without explicit request

## Forbidden
- Do not add npm packages without explicit request
- Do not change Prisma schema without explicit request
- Do not change folder structure
- Do not use inline styles
- Do not commit .env files

## Naming conventions
- Components: PascalCase (UserCard.tsx)
- Hooks: use + camelCase (useAuth.ts)
- Folders: kebab-case (user-profile/)

## API route pattern
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  try {
    const body = await req.json()
    const data = Schema.parse(body)
    return Response.json({ success: true })
  } catch (error) {
    return Response.json({ error: 'Server error' }, { status: 400 })
  }
}

## Auth check in API routes
const token = req.cookies.get('token')?.value
if (!token) return Response.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 })

## AI-first workflow tips
- Always check existing components before creating new ones
- Reuse UI Kit components from components/ui/ and shared/ui-kit/
- Keep API routes thin — move logic to features/
- Use Zustand for global state, TanStack Query for server state
